@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;motion] shared-navigation-keeps-one-compose-stack
Android and iOS MUST use the same Compose route stack and navigation callbacks for
shared screens. Following a link or opening a repository MUST append a route to that
stack; native Back adapters MUST pop the same stack, without rebuilding the underlying
page state. Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS plan and DESIGN.md
rules 88, 105 and 123.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security;architecture] native-entry-constructs-only-its-selected-workspace
A fresh iOS entry MUST mount the existing public GuestPages and tokenless session
without constructing private account discovery, Home, AI, Stats, settings sync or
usage observers. A matching locally verified existing connection MAY return to its
private workspace; restored preferences or Keychain tokens alone MUST NOT prove a
fresh installation belongs there. An explicit Explore choice MUST preserve saved
credentials and synchronously settle/retire private services, callbacks, palette
state and route/saveable owners before public pages mount. Both entries MUST use
the same supplied AppNavigation; returning to an entry MUST create a fresh source
without reviving its old callbacks or input. Strict Debug private fixtures MUST NOT
gain a public/network route. An ordinary checking or failed existing connection MUST
keep an explicit route back to public browsing. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 fresh-install/public browsing
decision and the accepted 22 Oct 2026 lazy iOS Guest integration plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] native-entry-handoff-keeps-the-displayed-link
Choosing the existing-server entry from a displayed guest link fallback MUST retain
that exact destination through private verification/sign-in on the same stack. A
newer incoming arrival MUST take precedence, and an old private audience MUST still
be enforced after verification. Entry selection MUST NOT copy a raw Guest repository
or review route into the private stack before the restored arrival passes that
audience check. Source: shared-incoming-links-keep-their-audience,
guest-incoming-links-commit-before-consumption and the accepted 22 Oct 2026 iOS mount.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] shared-back-cancels-current-edit-first
The single native edge-back observer MUST dispatch to the current page's active inline
edit before popping the shared route stack. A hidden page or an edit removed during
the gesture MUST NOT consume it or cause a route pop. Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026
iOS plan's native gesture adapter and preservation of Android's edit BackHandler.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture;motion] shared-dialog-native-progress-keeps-one-back-owner
A native Compose dialog's framework swipe MUST dispatch progress, cancellation and
completion through the same captured SharedBackDispatcher consumer used by its
sheet/edit controls. It MUST handle a root modal even when no application route can
pop. A cancelled gesture, removed/covered consumer or disposed bridge MUST NOT dismiss
its replacement or fall through to a route pop. Discrete Back MUST still select the
current shared consumer. The bridge MUST recheck the native host's same scene,
root-controller and presented-controller authority before every stage; absent or
revoked authority MUST fail closed without reacquiring a consumer in that gesture.
Source: Tavi's complete native journey request and the
accepted 22 Oct 2026 limitation-sheet Back completion repair, preserving DESIGN.md
rules 78 and 115 and shared-back-cancels-current-edit-first.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] shared-root-retires-private-source-before-replacement
The native account source's before-change hook MUST revoke its root lifetime, cancel
source work and clear Home, review caches and private route/saveable owners before a
replacement usable credential snapshot is published. Ordinary same-source navigation
MUST retain that application owner and its state. Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026
iOS account verification, source isolation and single shared-navigation plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-ai-host-policy-precedes-work
AI components MUST consult the same host capabilities before exposing mutation or
paid-work controls. A host without complete result readers MUST NOT start invisible
work; enabling analysis MUST include the existing Standard/Deep Brief result chain.
Android MUST retain its complete existing controls. Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026
iOS reuse plan, preserving the existing AI preset chains and complete task outcomes.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-review-write-policy-keeps-server-permissions
Shared review components MUST check the host's actual renderer/action readiness before
exposing or invoking writes. Host readiness MUST NOT replace the existing session's
server permission checks. A host without the complete comment, review or edit flow
MUST leave those mutation controls unavailable, while Android retains its existing
complete actions. Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS shared-review reuse plan and
its requirement to gate unsupported actions before RPC.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] shared-viewer-progress-has-workflow-readiness
The host's Reviewed and automatic next-file workflow MUST have an explicit readiness
capability before exposing or invoking progress mutations. Viewer progress MUST NOT
require GitHub comment or pull-request write permission. Android MUST retain its
existing complete workflow. Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS reuse plan's actual
review journey and the existing session.setReviewed viewer-progress semantics.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;motion] shared-review-back-follows-the-existing-nested-page
The review frame's nested page motion MUST consume the root's single native edge
gesture before the application route stack. It MUST follow gesture progress, return
on cancellation and leave the underlying route unchanged on commit. A removed or
covered consumer MUST NOT turn its gesture into another page's Back. Source: Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS plan and DESIGN.md rules 88, 93, 105 and 123.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] shared-commands-retire-private-owner
The host MUST close its Commands owner before replacement credentials become usable.
Retirement MUST clear the palette's query, expanded groups and scope. Retained rows,
keyboard actions and disposed page callbacks MUST NOT run through a retired owner;
closing the palette MUST recheck that owner before invoking a command. Android's
source observer MUST replay changes between owner capture and registration. Source:
Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 source isolation and shared Commands implementation plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] shared-incoming-links-keep-their-audience
An incoming intent MUST use the same Compose navigation stack and retain its file,
line, side, thread, commit, check and saved-result destination. An intent captured for
one configured endpoint, Access policy or signed-in account MUST NOT open for another.
A same-endpoint signed-out intent MAY wait for verified sign-in. Routing MUST recheck
the current source and arrival after closing sheets; a newer arrival MUST NOT be lost.
The audience check MUST precede any suspending sheet exit; a rejected old-source
intent MUST NOT close the current source's Settings, readers or transient controls.
Rejected native envelopes MUST report one invalid-link event without retaining their
URL. Source retirement MUST discard delivered reopen events; a pending sign-in intent
MAY remain only with its opening audience still enforced.
Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS link and account isolation plan and the existing
nav-link-closes-what-was-open and pr-links-land-on-the-thing requirements.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] shared-root-sheets-share-one-source-lifetime
The root MUST retain one Settings, model/catalog, Stats, Feedback and Commands bundle
for its active Home source. Ordinary navigation and sheet dismissal MUST retain that
bundle and unsent feedback. Before replacement credentials become usable, root
retirement MUST close the old bundle, clear one-time keys and feedback, and revoke
retained commands. A bundle that loses its source while being constructed MUST be
closed without being installed. Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 single shared
app lifetime and source-isolated account/Settings implementation plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] review-actions-read-live-readiness-before-fresh-work
Retained Review, Diff, AI setup, Brief, Chat, findings, progress, Undo and command
controls MUST intersect their drawn capability with the host's live source and
foreground readiness before a new request or queued next write. Synchronous
revocation MUST take effect before recomposition. This action gate MUST NOT retire
the session or its full view, clear drafts, cancel accepted requests or stop remote
work. Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 complete iOS journeys and shared lifecycle
plan, preserving shared-review-scene-stop-pauses-local-observation.
Temporary foreground revocation MUST NOT remove an installed same-view form's
remembered private input. Confirmed writes MUST settle their success or failure
under their captured source/view and actual installation policy, even while new
dispatch is paused. Accepted history restoration MUST survive its sheet's ordinary
close and wait for verified read authority before reopening Ask. Source: the
independent 21 Oct 2026 complete frame-action review and its three accepted fixes.
That accepted reconciliation MUST observe full-view and installation-policy retirement
throughout every paused read or resume wait, including a second pause during its
post-write saved-state read. Retirement MUST release the accepted change without
requiring foreground resume or starting its queued question. Source: the accepted
22 Oct 2026 independent frame-receipt read-wait review.
